  "description": "A from-scratch rich text editor control for WinUI 3, rendered with Win2D (CanvasVirtualControl / CanvasTextLayout). A port of AvaloniaRichEditor: text/paragraph formatting, tables (nested, colspan/rowspan, resize), inline & block images, hyperlinks, undo/redo, CJK/Korean IME, clipboard (rich/HTML/RTF), page view, print/PDF, find, and drop-in host controls. Byte-compatible .flow document format. Native AOT ready.",
  "id": "WinUIRichEditor",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-07-31T15:09:09.64Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "TJboPDIWrFQezkF+g7XnGDB8ILddL6GRxC6RyQT8AIr/FWZXh+ca86z4RIBJRKlKEZqE/4XC/p2SLzT4JoeLGA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 244427,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/centwon/WinUIRichEditor",
  "published": "2026-07-31T15:05:59.603Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "See CHANGELOG.md. 1.0.0 freezes the public API: from here on it follows SemVer, and the surface is tracked in PublicAPI.Shipped.txt so a change to it cannot ship unnoticed. What made this 1.0 is verification depth, not new features — a full comparison against AvaloniaRichEditor 1.0 fixed 20 defects, including two memory-exhaustion DoS paths reachable from a paste (HTML colspan, JSON/.flow declared table size), text loss when importing ordinary Word RTF, and a toolbar that silently took keyboard focus away from the editor. BREAKING: Formatters.RoundTripHarness is gone (a development tool; it moved to the demo). BEHAVIOUR: a damaged document now throws (InvalidDataException / JsonException) instead of reading as an empty one, so hosts calling LoadJson/LoadJsonAsync/LoadPackageAsync must handle it — reading a damaged file as empty meant the next save overwrote a recoverable file. RTF table output changed shape for HWP fidelity (horizontal merge is geometric; tables nested in a cell are real \\itap nesting), and inline tables now survive an HTML/RTF round trip. Added: nine behaviour flags became dependency properties (bindable), XML documentation now ships with the package.",
